---
source: system/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: "help_output(\"lsmem\")"
---
List the ranges of available memory with their online status

Usage: lsmem [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -a, --all                List each individual memory block
  -b, --bytes              Print SIZE in bytes rather than human-readable format
  -J, --json               Use JSON output format
  -n, --noheadings         Don't print headings
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>    Output columns to print
      --output-all         Output all available columns
  -P, --pairs              Use key="value" output format
  -r, --raw                Use raw output format
  -S, --split <SPLIT>      Split ranges by specified columns
  -s, --sysroot <SYSROOT>  Use specified directory as system root
      --summary <SUMMARY>  Print summary information (never, always, only) [default: always]
  -h, --help               Print help
